<title>UK: Rank shares fall on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Rank shares fall on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rank Organisation Plc fell prey to profit-taking following last week's jump on news the UK leisure group would buy back shares and sell its stake in Rank Xerox to Xerox Corp, traders said.</p>
<p>Rank fell eight pence to 440-1/2, after having advanced 26 pence on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Some people take profits, others think Friday's gain was overdone,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Turnover in the shares was 4.45 million by 1120 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
